<DocsLayout title="Interception &amp; Rewriting" description="Minimal examples for every rewriting capability">
  <h1>Interception &amp; Rewriting Capabilities</h1>

  <p>Each example below is a Rule JSON that <code>relay-core rules validate</code> accepts (and that <code>PUT /api/v1/rules</code> stores). The shape matches the <a href="/en/docs/rule-engine">Rule API</a>: <code>active</code>, <code>stage</code>, <code>termination</code>, a tagged <code>filter</code>, and an <code>actions</code> array. Action fields live under <code>config</code>.</p>

  <h2 id="mock-response">Mock Response</h2>
  <p>Replace the upstream response with a local one. Useful for frontend work, contract tests, and error simulation. Stopping at the request-header stage means the upstream is never contacted.</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "mock-health",
  "name": "Mock /v1/health",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "RequestHeaders",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Stop",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Path", "config": &#123; "mode": "Exact", "value": "/v1/health" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123;
    "type": "MockResponse",
    "config": &#123;
      "status": 200,
      "headers": &#123; "content-type": "application/json" &#125;,
      "body": &#123; "type": "Text", "value": "&#123;\\"ok\\":true&#125;" &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2 id="map-local">Map Local</h2>
  <p>Serve the request from a local file. The path must stay inside the policy sandbox root.</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "map-local-static",
  "name": "Serve /static from disk",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "RequestHeaders",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Stop",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Path", "config": &#123; "mode": "Prefix", "value": "/static/" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123;
    "type": "MapLocal",
    "config": &#123; "path": "/Users/me/projects/app/static", "content_type": null &#125;
  &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2 id="map-remote">Map Remote</h2>
  <p>Rewrite the request URL to another origin.</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "map-remote-prod-to-staging",
  "name": "api.example.com -&gt; staging",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "RequestHeaders",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Stop",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Host", "config": &#123; "mode": "Exact", "value": "api.example.com" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123;
    "type": "MapRemote",
    "config": &#123; "url": "https://api-staging.example.com", "preserve_host": false &#125;
  &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2 id="redirect">Redirect</h2>
  <p>Return a 3xx redirect.</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "redirect-legacy",
  "name": "/old -&gt; /new",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "RequestHeaders",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Stop",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Path", "config": &#123; "mode": "Exact", "value": "/old" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123;
    "type": "Redirect",
    "config": &#123; "location": "https://example.com/new", "status": 301 &#125;
  &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2 id="header-modification">Header modification</h2>
  <p>Add, update, or delete request and response headers. <code>UpdateRequestHeader</code> / <code>UpdateResponseHeader</code> accept <code>&#123;&#123;previous&#125;&#125;</code> in <code>value</code>.</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "strip-cookie",
  "name": "Strip Set-Cookie on /api/*",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "ResponseHeaders",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Continue",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Path", "config": &#123; "mode": "Prefix", "value": "/api/" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123; "type": "DeleteResponseHeader", "config": &#123; "name": "set-cookie" &#125; &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "add-debug",
  "name": "Add X-Debug header",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "RequestHeaders",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Continue",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Method", "config": &#123; "mode": "Exact", "value": "POST" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123;
    "type": "AddRequestHeader",
    "config": &#123; "name": "x-debug", "value": "relay-core" &#125;
  &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2 id="body-modification">Body modification</h2>
  <p>Replace a body, run a regex, or set a JSONPath. Body-dependent rules belong on <code>RequestBody</code> / <code>ResponseBody</code>. A body over the inspect budget is skipped with a recorded reason; it is not matched against the truncated prefix.</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "jsonpath-set",
  "name": "Force user.role = admin",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "RequestBody",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Continue",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Host", "config": &#123; "mode": "Exact", "value": "api.example.com" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123;
    "type": "TransformRequestBody",
    "config": &#123;
      "transform": &#123;
        "type": "JsonPathSet",
        "config": &#123; "path": "$.user.role", "value": "\\"admin\\"" &#125;
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "regex-replace",
  "name": "Replace token in body",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "ResponseBody",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Continue",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Path", "config": &#123; "mode": "Exact", "value": "/login" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123;
    "type": "TransformResponseBody",
    "config": &#123;
      "transform": &#123;
        "type": "RegexReplace",
        "config": &#123; "pattern": "secret=([^&amp;]+)", "replacement": "secret=REDACTED" &#125;
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2 id="intercept-breakpoints">Intercept breakpoints</h2>
  <p>Pause live traffic for a human decision. Create a breakpoint with <code>POST /api/v1/intercepts</code> or MCP <code>set_intercept</code>; release or drop it with <code>resume</code> / <code>resume_flow</code>. There is no <code>relay-core intercept</code> subcommand.</p>

  <pre><code>curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/v1/intercepts \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '&#123;
    "url_pattern": "api.example.com",
    "phase": "request"
  &#125;'</code></pre>

  <p>Hits show up in the TUI <strong>Intercepts</strong> panel and via <code>GET /api/v1/intercepts</code>. <code>request_header_upserts</code> / <code>response_header_upserts</code> add or overwrite by name and keep the rest. <code>request_headers</code> / <code>response_headers</code> replace the whole header map.</p>

  <pre><code>curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/v1/intercepts/&lt;key&gt;/resume \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '&#123;
    "action": "continue",
    "request_header_upserts": &#123; "x-test": "value" &#125;
  &#125;'</code></pre>

  <p>Modifiable fields: <code>method</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>request_headers</code>, <code>request_header_upserts</code>, <code>request_body</code>, <code>status_code</code>, <code>response_headers</code>, <code>response_header_upserts</code>, <code>response_body</code>, <code>message_content</code> (WebSocket).</p>

  <h2 id="flow-replay">Flow replay</h2>
  <p>Re-send a captured HTTP request as it was stored. This call cannot edit headers or body. The replay enters through the running proxy, so it is captured as a new flow and the current rules and scripts apply. The call fails when the proxy is not running. HTTP only; WebSocket flows are rejected.</p>
  <pre><code>curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/v1/flows/&lt;id&gt;/replay

# Skip TLS verification (debug only)
curl -X POST 'http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/v1/flows/&lt;id&gt;/replay?accept_invalid_certs=true'</code></pre>

  <h2>WebSocket message rewriting</h2>
  <p>Two actions apply only at stage <code>WebSocketMessage</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "ws-mock",
  "name": "Mock chat messages",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "WebSocketMessage",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Stop",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "Host", "config": &#123; "mode": "Exact", "value": "chat.example.com" &#125; &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123;
    "type": "MockWebSocketMessage",
    "config": &#123;
      "direction": "Incoming",
      "message": "&#123;\\"type\\":\\"welcome\\",\\"user\\":\\"bot\\"&#125;"
    &#125;
  &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <p>Or drop matching messages:</p>
  <pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "ws-drop-pings",
  "name": "Drop ping frames",
  "active": true,
  "stage": "WebSocketMessage",
  "priority": 100,
  "termination": "Stop",
  "filter": &#123; "type": "All" &#125;,
  "actions": [&#123; "type": "DropWebSocketMessage" &#125;]
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2>L3/L4 actions</h2>
  <p>These three actions only apply at the <code>Connect</code> stage:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>RedirectIp</code> — dial a different IP</li>
    <li><code>ForwardPort</code> — forward to another host:port (hostnames are resolved)</li>
    <li><code>SetTtl</code> — accepted, then logged; the TTL on the wire does not change</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
